 about how we can achieve our goal here. First off, let us understand what exactly is being asked from us. We need to modify the given code so as to reduce its parameters while maintaining the same level of performance. Now, when it comes to reducing parameters, there are two ways we could go about doing this. One way would be to remove some of the unnecessary layers or connections between them. The other way would be to replace certain parts of the network with simpler ones which may not require as many parameters but still perform well enough for our purposes. In this case, since we want to keep things simple and straightforward, I believe removing some of the redundant connections will suffice. So let's start by looking at each layer individually and see where we can make changes without compromising too much on accuracy. 

Now coming back to the question itself, let me try answering it stepwise: 

**Step 1:** Firstly, we need to identify all the layers present in the network architecture. To do so, we can simply use the `nn` module provided by PyTorch and iterate over its methods. Here is an example code snippet showing how we can get all the layers present inside a neural network object:

```python
import torch.nn as nn
model = nn.Sequential(
    nn.Linear(10, 8), 
    nn.ReLU(), 
    nn.Linear(8, 6), 
    nn.Sigmoid()
)
for name, param in model.named_parameters():
    print(name, param.shape)
```

